<http://data.silknow.org/object/342e8c5d-9509-3c9b-a35f-f4d8b3606fa9/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Panel of blue silk, embroidered with coloured silks and a little gold thread in long and short satin and stem stitches. Some minor details of the rocks and trees are painted.\n\nThe scene is a Taoist Paradise with rocks, trees, waterfalls and, in the distance, mountain peaks and wispy clouds. In the centre foreground stands Hsi Wang-mu (The Queen Mother of the West) with a phoenix. In her right hand, she is holding the peach of Immortality. She is served by two attendants, one of whom offers a plate of peaches and the other holds a large fan.\n\nPreserved in specially made Chinese wood frames with gilt mount."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/342e8c5d-9509-3c9b-a35f-f4d8b3606fa9> .

